stream
DAY 3 DEVELOPER SUPPORT FILES
These files are embedded in the solved PDF. In a PDF reader with an
Attachments panel, save all files to one folder. No extra pages replace
the workbook. The completed printed answer fields are self-contained.

developer_extensions.py: Task 1 validation, Task 2 cleaning, Task 3
analysis/charts/Excel export, Task 4 API classifier (10 records/call),
Task 6 generate_sales_report(csv_path, week_date, region).
test_developer.py: mocked report structure/weekly filtering and classifier
10+5 batching/invalid-ID handling. Neither test calls the real API.
sales.csv: exact sample sales. sales_clean.csv: 20 records + 2 flags.
feedback.csv: exact feedback text with PDF line wrapping removed.
feedback_classified_sample.csv: this session's reviewed classifications,
not output from a live gpt-4o-mini API call.
n8n_conceptual.json: Task 8 node/connection design, NOT import-ready.
analysis_report.xlsx and the two PNG charts: local Task 3 script outputs.

Requirements: Python 3.10+, pandas, matplotlib, openpyxl.
Local validation/cleaning/analysis: python developer_extensions.py local
Mocked tests: python test_developer.py
Optional API classifier: set OPENAI_API_KEY securely, then explicitly run
python developer_extensions.py classify
Sales report usage from Python:
from developer_extensions import generate_sales_report
report = generate_sales_report('sales.csv', '2024-03-01', 'All')

week_date is the first day of a seven-day period. The workbook's full
sample report covers 1-15 March; the function example covers 1-7 March.
API key is never embedded. The API routines have not been live-tested.
They do not send messages to colleagues or modify external tickets.
Human review remains required for labels, figures and draft actions.
Savings and peer feedback in the PDF are explicitly illustrative.

Official references for API request shape and requested model:
https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat/create
https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-4o-mini

endstream
endobj
